   "author": "Adam Crawley",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/adam-crawley-b2146753_the-demand-side-of-our-order-book-moved-in-activity-7519538986156056576-u6yE",
   "text": "The demand side of our order book moved in Q3 and it moved toward hardware. \n\nRanked by growth in buy-side orders versus Q2, the top four in Augment\u2019s Power 20 were Impulse Space, Etched, Hadrian and Blue Origin, so two space companies, a chip company and a manufacturer, with The Boring Company, Replit, Cognition and Kalshi behind them.\n\nWhat's interesting from an execution standpoint is that demand often shows up in a name before the sellers do. Buyers read the news and want in, and the shareholders who could sell are often employees and early investors who may not be in a hurry, so for a quarter or two you may see a lot of bids and a thin offer and the spread tells you that.\n\nSpace and man",
