  "7519604073243836416": {
   "created": 1792813318,
   "author": "Parallax \u200e",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/parallax001_people-talk-about-large-language-models-like-activity-7519604073243836416-CytN",
   "text": "People talk about large language models like they are complex software organisms with hidden reasoning gears inside. If you actually open up the source code of a frontier transformer, over 99% of the compute time is spent running the exact same high-school math operation six times in a row.\n\nThe entire trillion-dollar AI industry is basically a giant wrapper around a single hardware instruction: GEMM (General Matrix Multiply).\n\nWhen you type a word into a model, it immediately converts that word into a list of numbers\u2014say, 4,096 floating-point values that capture its meaning in space. From that moment on, the chip doesn't know what English is. It just pushes that 4,096-number array through a",
